1
00:00:00,217 --> 00:00:02,217
(Sheldon:)Maybe it's a new planet.

2
00:00:02,219 --> 00:00:04,619
(Raj:)Unlikely, but it could be
a dwarf planet.

3
00:00:04,621 --> 00:00:06,151
(Sheldon:)Well, as long as it has
a healthy gravity

4
00:00:06,156 --> 00:00:07,726
(Sheldon:)and all its moons,
I'll be happy.

5
00:00:07,724 --> 00:00:11,694
(Raj:)Okay, the final image
is coming in.

6
00:00:11,695 --> 00:00:13,665
(Raj:)And the object
we discovered is...

7
00:00:13,663 --> 00:00:15,063
(Sheldon:)Come on,

8
00:00:15,065 --> 00:00:19,065
(Sheldon:)Daddy needs a livable planet
he can rule with an iron fist.

9
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:21,740
(Raj:)A medium-sized asteroid.

10
00:00:21,738 --> 00:00:23,138
(Sheldon:)That's it?

11
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:24,640
(Sheldon:)How common.

12
00:00:24,641 --> 00:00:28,181
(Sheldon:)That's the chicken fingers
on the menu of space.

13
00:00:28,178 --> 00:00:29,948
(Raj:)I kind of like chicken fingers.

14
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:32,516
(Sheldon:)Yeah, me, too.
I was stuck for a metaphor.

15
00:00:32,516 --> 00:00:34,846
(Sheldon:)Come on,
a medium-sized asteroid

16
00:00:34,851 --> 00:00:36,781
(Raj:)is still
an interesting discovery.

17
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:38,486
(Sheldon:)I suppose it
could end up

18
00:00:38,488 --> 00:00:42,288
(Sheldon:)on a collision course with Earth
and destroy life as we know it.

19
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:44,862
(Raj:)You dream different than me.

20
00:00:46,696 --> 00:00:48,396
(Sheldon:)It is kind of cute.

21
00:00:48,398 --> 00:00:50,568
(Raj:)Yeah, it is.
And you know we get to name it.

22
00:00:50,567 --> 00:00:51,697
(gasps)

23
00:00:51,701 --> 00:00:54,071
(Sheldon:)We better choose a name
no one can make fun of.

24
00:00:54,070 --> 00:01:01,020
(Sheldon:)Sir Frederick William Herschel
didn't do Uranus any favors.

